ce 1907, the warmest since 2025.","t_yest":"November 13: warmer than 84% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>62\u00b0F</strong> was the 18th warmest November 13 high (tied) of 120 since 1907, the warmest since 2025. The normal high for the date is 49\u00b0F, and the record is 76\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>25\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Sheridan is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Sheridan's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Sheridan has set <strong>58 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 82 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">149 record highs</strong>, far more than the 82 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (67). Sheridan's all-time high is 109\u00b0F, on July 12, 2026.","t_chg":"Sheridan has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 118 complete years: Sheridan's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +0.25), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1908. Sheridan's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.27\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.38), about +3.2\u00b0F since 1908.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Sheridan's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.14 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 14.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 1923 (29.79 in); the driest, 1960 (8.23 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 16 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}